PackageIdentifier: dagsommer.boks
PackageVersion: {{VERSION}}
PackageLocale: en-US
Publisher: Dag Sommer
PublisherUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer
PublisherSupportUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer/boks/issues
Author: Dag Sommer
PackageName: Boks
PackageUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer/boks
License: Apache-2.0
LicenseUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer/boks/blob/main/LICENSE
ShortDescription: Run coding agents and other untrusted developer tooling in local microVMs
Description: >-
  Boks runs coding agents and other untrusted developer tooling inside isolated microVMs on
  your own machine. It is a local-first, open-source alternative to Docker Sandboxes — no
  account, no cloud service, no telemetry.

  Each sandbox is a real virtual machine with its own kernel, not a container sharing yours,
  and every network flow out of it is judged against a policy you set before it is dialled.
  Your workspace is shared into the guest at its exact host path; nothing else is.

  On Windows the microVM runs on the Windows Hypervisor Platform. This is not WSL2 and needs
  no elevated terminal. Boks is experimental: read the project's verification record for what
  has been measured rather than what the feature list implies.
Moniker: boks
Tags:
- agent
- cli
- containerd
- developer-tools
- hypervisor
- isolation
- microvm
- sandbox
- security
- virtualization
ReleaseNotesUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer/boks/releases/tag/v{{VERSION}}
Documentations:
- DocumentLabel: Installing Boks
  DocumentUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer/boks/blob/main/docs/install.md
- DocumentLabel: What has actually been verified
  DocumentUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer/boks/blob/main/docs/verification.md
- DocumentLabel: Boks on Windows
  DocumentUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer/boks/blob/main/docs/windows.md
InstallationNotes: |-
  Open a new terminal so the `boks` alias is on PATH, then:

    boks doctor          check every prerequisite and print a remedy for each gap
    boks daemon start    start the containerd this package ships, configured for Boks
    boks run shell .     run a sandbox over the current directory

  This package is not code-signed. Windows SmartScreen may warn the first time you run
  boks.exe; see docs/install.md for why, and for how to verify the download instead.
ManifestType: defaultLocale
ManifestVersion: 1.12.0
